<title>UK: Cazenove Indian GDR Index down 3.8 percent.</title>
<headline>Cazenove Indian GDR Index down 3.8 percent.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Cazenove Indian GDR Index fell 2.4 points, 3.8 percent, to 60.2 after the Bombay Stock Exchange 30 share index closed down 52.94 points at 2,754.06.</p>
<p>The premium for GDRs over stocks on the local market was 13.23 percent.</p>
<p>The Cazenove index is a capitalisation weighted basket of Indian global depositary receipts and measures the change from midday on the previous trading day to midday today.</p>
<p>-- David Chance, London Newsroom +44 171 542 5887</p>
